{"duration_api_ms":150323,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"67ef537a-71e9-41bc-a64c-0e8988269b0c","total_cost_usd":0.8866976,"usage":{"input_tokens":30,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55365,"cache_read_input_tokens":1041088,"output_tokens":11772,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1068},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":55365,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1121,"cache_read_input_tokens":86059,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1644,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1644},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":30,"outputTokens":11772,"cacheReadInputTokens":1041088,"cacheCreationInputTokens":55365,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8866976,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1068,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":55365,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":15,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the round 2 diagnosis for x2t, recorded the measurements and committed it (`024b052`). All acceptance commands pass, `theseus validate` shows no errors, and `theseus scope-check` is clean. The differential oracle failed on my first run and passed on the second; see below.\n\n**What round 1 actually delivered:** no change to x2t's code. `external/core` and `external/core.base` are at the same commit, so the oracle builds one x2t and runs it on both sides. Round 1's speed gains exist only as patches:\n- **V8 startup snapshots** cut about 0.1 s per PDF. They ship only as a packaging patch and are active only on this VM.\n- **The text-shaping cache** cut 13–24 % of the time on very large spreadsheets. It is a patch to sdkjs (the editor's JavaScript), not to x2t, and has no pull request yet.\n\nI counted both as not delivered.\n\n**Differential oracle (original vs new):**\n- **Run 1:** the direct comparison passed, but the browser half failed with 7 differences, all on `text-10p.docx`. Both sides were the same binary. The scripted edit sometimes finishes after the capture (\"Local edit old\" instead of \"Local edit bold\"). So this is noise in the test, not a real difference.\n- **Run 2:** passed completely. The browser half therefore fails intermittently (1 of 2 runs here), and each run takes about 10 minutes.\n\n**Measurements** (in `.theseus/oracle/rounds/x2t-r2.md`): converting an empty template to PDF still takes 0.68–1.25 s, against about 0.12 s for opening, saving or converting to ODF. That gap is a fixed cost every user pays on a PDF export, and it is all inside x2t. Timings varied by up to 2× between the two runs because other agents were using the machine, so read them as proportions.\n\n**Verdict: refactor, in C++, conditional on a stable oracle.** The remaining fixed cost is the first JavaScript run inside a fresh V8 engine in every x2t process. The core fork is now writable, so this round can change the code. The plan for round 2:\n- **P1:** fix the edit race in `x2t-run.cjs` so the browser oracle stops failing on its own noise.\n- **P2:** profile that first run with snapshots on, and try two fixes in the core fork: taking the snapshot after a warm-up run, and changing V8 flags.\n- **P3:** implement the better option in `doctrenderer.cpp`, aiming for at least 0.3 s less per PDF.\n\nKeeping one x2t process alive between conversions is deferred. It would change the contract with FileConverter, so I'd only consider it if P2's options gain less than 0.2 s.\n\n**Notes:** `DIAG-x2t-b.md` did not exist, so there was nothing to `git rm`. I did not edit the oracle, which is outside my target; fixing it is P1. The executor log and the friction line are written.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- Round 1's gains were real but never merged or shipped, which is why the module gained nothing. The method has no field to mark work that exists only as a patch; I noted that in the friction line.\n- The x2t browser oracle is flaky and needs fixing before it can judge a real change to core.","ttft_ms":3890,"type":"result","duration_ms":1821037,"uuid":"85889218-978e-44b1-aa8d-f400c6422c2a","ttft_stream_ms":2529,"time_to_request_ms":282,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":153,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":25,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":11,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":8,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":18,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":5,"request_build":10},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":121,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":159,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":211,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":230,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":246,"process_cpu_ms_turn":12546,"process_wall_ms_turn":1821036,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1722,"process_wall_ms_streaming":100773,"main_stream_count":15,"main_stream_event_count":1874,"main_stream_chunk_count":1433,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":1722,"wall_ms":100773,"entries":15},"tool